 "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/bfee7f279e97a59b.png\" alt=\"The comparative table shows the relation of the Port of New Orleans to the Panama Canal and Pacific Ocean Ports. The following distances are in nautical miles from New Orleans: to San Francisco via the Panama Canal, 4,704 nautical miles; to San Francisco via Straits of Magellan, 13,539 nautical miles; to Manila, Philippine Islands via the Panama Canal, Honolulu, and Guam, 10,935 nautical miles; to Manila, Philippine Islands via the Suez Canal, 12,946 nautical miles; to Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands via the Panama Canal, 6,095 nautical miles; to Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands via the Straits of Magellan, 13,719 nautical miles; to Yokohama, Japan via Panama Canal and Honolulu, 9,537 nautical miles; to Yokohama, Japan via Suez and Singapore, 14,471 nautical miles; to Hong Kong, China via the Panama Canal and Honolulu, 11,009 nautical miles; to Hong Kong China via the Straits of Magellan and Apia, 17,405 nautical miles; to Melbourne, Australia via the Panama Canal and direct, 9,427 nautical miles; to Melbourne, Australia via the Cape of Good Hope, 12,933 nautical miles. The following distances are from New York: to San Francisco via the Panama Canal, 5,305 nautical miles; to San Francisco via Straits of Magellan, 13,089 nautical miles; to Manila, Philippine Islands via the Panama Canal, Honolulu, and Guam, 11,536 nautical miles; to Manila, Philippine Islands via the Suez Canal, 11,556 nautical miles; to Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands via the Panama Canal, 6,696 nautical miles; to Honolulu Hawaiian Islands via the Straits of Magellan, 13,269 nautical miles; to Yokohama, Japan via the Panama Canal and Honolulu, 10,138 nautical miles; to Yokohama, Japan via Suez and Singapore, 13,040 nautical miles; to Hong Kong, China via the Panama Canal and Honolulu, 11,610 nautical miles; to Hong Kong China via the Straits of Magellan and Apia, 16,955 nautical miles; to Melbourne, Australia via the Panama Canal and direct, 10,028 nautical miles; to Melbourne, Australia via the Cape of Good Hope, 12,670 nautical miles.\">\n<figcaption>This 1912 table compares the distance between New York, New Orleans, and Pacific Ocean ports via different oceanic routes including the Panama Canal.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p><i>Refer to the image provided.</i></p>",
